WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.590
The losses of Infinity War were devastating,
but the surviving heroes aren't giving up

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:05.300
without a fight.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:10.080
Clint Barton, aka Hawkeye, is coming back
to help finish the job in round two, Avengers:

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:10.580
Endgame.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:14.780
But this time around, he's bringing a different,
darker attitude, and perhaps even a whole

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:15.300
new name.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.700
Here's why this overlooked Avenger will be
more important than you think.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:20.160
Potential spoilers ahead!

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.000
Everything went wrong at the end of Infinity
War.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.340
Just like that, half the universe was dead
and dusted, including, we can assume, Clint

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:28.380
Barton's entire family.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:32.759
At least, that's what the first trailer for
Avengers: Endgame seems to want us to think,

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:36.730
cutting to Barton in the streets of Japan
while Captain America's voice over discusses

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:39.520
the family members people lost to Thanos'
decimation.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.840
This Clint looks like a man with a sunken
soul, a murderous mood, and nothing left to

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:44.340
lose.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:48.820
He's also got a kickass samurai-inspired new
outfit, with a sword as his weapon and no

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:49.660
arrows in sight.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:53.520
If you're familiar with his whole story in
the comics, you know he's probably not going

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:54.699
by Hawkeye anymore.

00:00:54.699 --> 00:00:57.499
That's right, folks, it's time to meet a new
hero.

00:00:57.499 --> 00:00:58.499
Goodbye, Hawkeye.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:00:59.380
Hello, Ronin.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:04.420
While he's more popularly known as Hawkeye,
Barton has taken on other names before, including

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:07.540
a brief stint as the size-changing Goliath
in the 1960s.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:12.680
In 2007, he took up the mantle of another
hero in the pages of The New Avengers, adopting

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:13.780
the role of Ronin.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:18.420
As Ronin, Barton showed off his combat skills
beyond the bow, taking coaching and encouragement

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:22.870
he had previously received from Captain America
and putting it to good use as a more well-rounded

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:23.360
fighter.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:27.060
After three years in the Ronin role, he returned
to his Hawkeye roots in 2010.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:32.020
While Comics Clint was in the Ronin identity,
he and the other Avengers faced off against

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:36.850
a new threat: the shape-shifting Skrulls,
aka why Captain Marvel punches an old lady

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:37.720
in those trailers.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:42.780
In this storyline, many superheroes and their
allies turn out to secretly be Skrulls, wearing

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:46.400
the faces of established heroes to further
a nefarious invasion plot.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:49.300
Ronin is one of the heroes who helps beat
the threat back.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.420
Considering the timing, we have to wonder,
is that what the movie Ronin is up to as well?

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:54.100
Maybe!

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:58.840
The "Ronin vs. Skrulls in Japan" rumors stem
from a casting notice for Endgame which called

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:03.170
for actors who were comfortable wearing facial
prosthetics, which could indicate a lot of

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:07.840
things besides an alien Skrull presence, since
this is a comic book movie we're talking about.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.560
Some online chatter indicates that Ronin will
play a huge role when it comes to ultimately

00:02:12.579 --> 00:02:17.150
defeating Thanos, which seems far-fetched,
considering Barton's recent absence in the

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:17.640
MCU.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:21.260
"You couldn't have done it without me."

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.500
But let's explore the speculation!

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:27.520
One Reddit-based rumor says that Ronin will
be involved with a plot to build a second

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:28.709
Infinity Gauntlet.

00:02:28.709 --> 00:02:32.780
After creating a second gauntlet, the Avengers
will hop through time to capture different

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:37.560
Infinity Stones before Thanos gets his hands
on them, something that, based on leaked location

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:42.090
photos of past setpieces being recreated for
Endgame, like the Battle of New York from

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:44.569
the first Avengers flick, seems very plausible.

00:02:44.569 --> 00:02:48.010
Specifically, it's rumored that Ronin will
have a scene in which he is forced to defend

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:50.030
the new gauntlet from Thanos' minions.

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:52.900
A perfect opportunity for Ronin to show off
his new skills.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:57.659
Regardless of whether or not Clint spends
Endgame fighting Skrulls or building a new

00:02:57.659 --> 00:03:01.529
golden glove, there's reason to believe he'll
be essential to setting up the next phase

00:03:01.529 --> 00:03:02.529
of the MCU.

00:03:02.529 --> 00:03:04.640
After all, Endgame is an end of an era.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:06.000
It's like Tony Stark says:

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.760
"Part of the journey is the end."

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:13.519
For the first time in series history, it's
time for a new generation of young Avengers

00:03:13.519 --> 00:03:17.060
to take over, and in the comics, Hawkeye has
one heck of a protégé.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:21.020
While Clint Barton is Marvel Comics' first
Hawkeye, he's not the only one.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:26.120
Since 2005, Barton has had a mentor/mentee
relationship with a younger archer named Kate

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:29.019
Bishop, an equally powerful wielder of the
bow and arrow.

00:03:29.019 --> 00:03:32.639
Since her first appearance in the pages of
Young Avengers, she's popped up in a wide

00:03:32.639 --> 00:03:37.189
array of Marvel comics, even headlining her
own series starting in 2016.

00:03:37.189 --> 00:03:41.440
It was reported in October that Katherine
Langford from 13 Reasons Why was secretly

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:44.020
cast in Endgame in an undisclosed role.

00:03:44.209 --> 00:03:47.900
We know what character she looks like, but
whether she'll pick up the bow as Kate Bishop

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:49.420
is still yet to be determined.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.960
Our thoughts are somewhere between "maybe"
and "probably."

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:55.640
Maybe Clint won't pass on his Hawkeye mantle
in Endgame.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:58.360
After all, there's already a lot going on
in this story.

00:03:58.360 --> 00:03:59.780
But what about what comes after?

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:04.480
MCU Cosmic reported that a project for the
upcoming Disney+ streaming service is being

00:04:04.489 --> 00:04:08.969
developed for the two Hawkeyes, with a plot
centering on Clint Barton training a successor

00:04:08.969 --> 00:04:11.919
who could, based on the comics, really only
be Kate Bishop.

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:15.160
In other words, we're pretty sure that Barton
is going to survive Endgame.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:19.200
And while he may retire afterwards, he won't
do it without passing on the bow to another

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:23.360
hero, one who will likely carry on his legacy
into MCU Phase 4 and beyond.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:27.660
It's worth remembering that these are still
just rumors and reports, with nothing official

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.820
announced, but keep an eye on these developments.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:33.280
Not only does it feel pretty believable, it
also sounds really, really fun.

